# Recap Class Activities
The class was began by the teacher asked us to create repository and branches. After, students took turn to answer questions from previous sessions. Then, we had a review on OOP which we discussed about function, Variables, Class, Method, Constant, Module, and Package. Variable is a named storage that used to store value or data. Function is a reusable block of code that performs or does specific task. Class is a blueprint or template that used to create objects and methods. Method is a function defined inside a class that belongs to an object. Constant is a value that remains fixed and unchanged througout the project. Module is a file or collection of files that groups related functions, variables, classes, or other logic into a reusable unit. Packages is a collection of related modules organized together inside a folder hierarchy. Last but not least, we discussed about clean code(maintaining consistency, proper indentation, useful or helpful comments). To keep our Python code clean, we should always aim to stick to the best practices outlined in the PEP 8 style guide.
